From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 18:00:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kk: transform feedback

VK_EXT_transform_feedback with geometryStreams, transform feedback
queries and vkCmdDrawIndirectByteCountEXT, on the geometry shader
emulation of the previous patch, as honeykrisp does it with poly:

- A geometry shader that captures keeps poly's count shader (when its
  counts are not static) and pre-GS program. Before the geometry shader
  runs, the count shader, a prefix sum of the counts (new
  libkk_prefix_sum_geom) and the pre-GS program set up each buffer's
  base for the draw, clamp to its size, advance the running offsets and
  add to the stream queries; the rasterization shader writes the
  captured vertices.
- A vertex or tess eval shader that captures, with no geometry shader,
  gets a passthrough geometry shader built into the pipeline (the point
  fill builder, generalised), which takes over its transform feedback
  layout.
- nir_lower_io does not annotate stores with transform feedback, so
  kk_lower_nir now does (nir_io_add_intrinsic_xfb_info). Without it the
  link-time varying optimization drops captured outputs the fragment
  shader does not read.
- Begin/End copy the running offsets from and to counter buffers on the
  GPU (libkk_copy_xfb_counters); DrawIndirectByteCount turns a counter
  into an indirect draw (libkk_draw_indirect_byte_count).
- VK_QUERY_TYPE_TRANSFORM_FEEDBACK_STREAM_EXT pools keep two reports
  per query (written, needed) at their own index, and
  vkCmdBegin/EndQueryIndexedEXT replace the unindexed entry points.
  Report addresses now use the pool's report stride and remap only
  occlusion query indices.
- A device-wide zero page and scratch page back poly's sink addresses:
  the offset of an inactive buffer reads zero, and writes through
  ro_to_rw_poly, and to counters of inactive queries, land in scratch.
  load_ro_sink_address_poly and load_rasterization_stream now come from
  the per-draw data.

Checked on the workstation only, on the mock Metal bridge: pipelines
that capture from a vertex, tess eval or geometry shader (dynamic
counts, two streams, rasterizing stream 1, lines, points, rasterizer
discard) build, their rasterization shaders write the captured
vertices, and Begin/End with counter buffers, resume,
DrawIndirectByteCount and the stream queries record and submit. Not run
on a GPU.

Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-26-kosmickrisp-xfb-host.md
Offered-upstream: no
